6. Give creators a clear progression

I’d organize the program into four stages.

Stage	Name	Objective
1	Discover	Choose a creative field, learn the tools, and meet potential teammates.
2	Build	Develop a prototype using AI-assisted workflows and collaborative production.
3	Launch	Publish a playable game, receive feedback, and participate in showcases or competitions.
4	Grow	Expand the game, pursue prizes and commercial opportunities, or establish an independent studio.

At each stage, the team should know what it needs to deliver and what opportunities become available after completion.

The commercial terms should be established before production, not introduced after the game becomes successful.

That is how we build trust.

