7. The rule I’d make official

Here’s the principle I would place in the Freedom World Creator Program Charter:

Creator Ownership, Commercial Opportunity, and Platform Continuity

Freedom World aims to provide creators with the tools, community, AI-assisted workflows, and collaborative environment needed to develop original games and creative projects.

Creators should have a meaningful opportunity to retain ownership of their original work, receive appropriate attribution, benefit financially from successful projects, and pursue independent publishing or commercial development.

For projects participating in the Freedom World Creator Partnership Program, Freedom World and the participating creators will establish written agreements before substantial production begins.

Those agreements will define intellectual-property ownership, platform licensing rights, revenue participation, contributor attribution, commercial publishing rights, and the conditions under which a game may be distributed outside Freedom World.

Freedom World intends to preserve a continuing economic and platform relationship with games developed through its partnership program while allowing creators to pursue broader opportunities under the agreed terms.

The program will seek to provide creators with the larger share of commercial proceeds when they perform the majority of the development work, with specific allocations determined by the applicable agreement.

Creators may use the skills and experience gained through participation to develop new projects, establish independent studios, and pursue other opportunities, subject to their contractual obligations and the intellectual-property rights of others.

Our objective is to build a sustainable creative ecosystem in which Freedom World, game creators, and the wider community can benefit from the development of original games.

